If I fix `field_annotation_is_sequence` and `field_annotation_is_complex`, then:
`field_annotation_is_sequence(Annotated[List[int], Meta])` -> `field_annotation_is_sequence(List[int])` -> `True`.
And `all(field_annotation_is_scalar(sub_annotation) for sub_annotation in get_args(Annotated[List[int], Meta]))`:
`get_args` returns `(List[int], Meta)`.
`field_annotation_is_scalar(List[int])` -> `not field_annotation_is_complex(List[int])` -> `not True` -> `False`.
So `field_annotation_is_scalar_sequence(Annotated[List[int], Meta])` will return `False`.
Which is correct, because `List[int]` is a sequence of scalars, but `Annotated[List[int], Meta]` is not a "scalar sequence" in the sense of the metadata being included in the args.

